  "identity": "English-language full-time Law in Society, 2026–2027. Adopted law faculty regulations and exact Study Guide courses establish the 180 EC programme, Recap and thesis progression, and zero-credit coaching. The OER uses R_RecPubl while the current Study Guide uses R_RecPubL for the same Recap title and credits. The formal wording and exact thesis entry list resolve the run-together public law and terrorism row.",
  "progression": "The English-taught full-time programme has ten compulsory 6 EC units in each of years one and two. Year three has 30 EC of open study, three 6 EC Recap courses and a 12 EC thesis. The Recap courses require 36 EC from eight specified legal and thematic units. Thesis entry requires Evaluation Research and 30 EC from specified legal, thematic and Recap units. The current thesis course lists Public Law and Terrorism separately where the regulations combine them typographically. Thesis assessment combines an individual legal and empirical study with a group empirical component and poster. English diagnostic completion or the refresher gates the Diversity grade. Professional and Personal Identity coaching carries no credits. Approved alternative elective or exchange packages are subject to course level and approval rules. Civiel Effect requires a separate Dutch preparatory pathway and a qualifying law master.",
